dbeedle@rs6000.cmp.ilstu.edu (Dave Beedle) writes: 

>
>  The hints say that you can throw food to a wild dog to make them happy.  
>How?  Say my poor kitty hits the trap door.  By the time I find it again it 
>doesn't like me.  Anyway to make them happy again?


Get in line with your pet (former).  Then throw, but instead of throwing
a weapon, use the letter of a tripe ration.  The food will miss the pet,
and the pet will chow down.  The pet is now friendly again.  You can
also use things like geckos, jackals, etc.  Anything that the pet would
eat normally.


Another thing throwing food is useful for is having your pet rob shops.
When your pet brings an item to you, you can throw food at it, and it
will learn - see Pavlov Dog Slalvation Theory.

